

Commends :
		- Cisco Discovery Protocol (CDP) 

			1. sh cdp
				---> Shows basic information about CDP (timers, version)

			2. sh cdp traffic
				---> Displays how many CDP messages have been sent and received 

			3. sh cdp int
				----> Display which int CDP is enabled on

			4. sh cdp neighbors
				----> List CDP neighbors and some basic information about each neighbor	

			5. sh cdp neighbors detail
				----> Lists each CDP neighbors with more detailed information 	
	
			6. sh cdp entry < device Id | Name >
				----> Displays the same info as above, but for the specified neighbors only

			7. R1(config)# [no] cdp run
				----> Enable / Disable CDP globally
			
			9. R1(config-if)# [no] cdp enable
				----> Enable / Disable CDP on specific int
		
			10. R1(config)# cdp timer seconds
				----> configure the cdp timer

			11. R1(config)# cdp holdtime seconds
				----> configure the cdp holdtime
			
			12. R1*config)# [no] cdp advertise-v2
				----> Enable / Disble CDPv2

		- Link Layer Discovery Protocol (LLDP)

			1. R1(config)# LLDP run
				---> enable LLDP globally

			2. R1(config-if)# LLDP transmit
				---> enable LLDP on specific interface

			3. R1(config-if)# LLDP receive
				---> enable LLDP on specific interface

			4. R1(config)# LLDP timer seconds
				---> LLDP timer seconds

			5. R1(config)# LLDP holdtime seconds
				---> LLDP holdtime

			6. R1(config)# LLDP reinit seconds
				---> LLDP reinit timer
			
			7. R1# show LLDP
				---> show basic information about LLDP (timer, version)

			8. R1# show LLDP traffic
				---> display how many LLDP messages have been sent and received

			9. R1# show LLDP interface
				---> Display which interface LLDP tx/rx is enabled on

			10. R1# show LLDP neighbors
				---> Lists LLDP neighbors and some basic information about each neighbor
	
			11. R1# show LLDP neighbors detail 
				---> list each LLDP neighbor with more detailed information
			
			12. R1# show LLDP entry name
				---> display the same info as above, but for the specified neighbor only
			
			

Things Covered :

		- Intro to layer 2 Discovery Protocols

		- Cisco Discovery Protocol (CDP)

		- Link Layer Discovery Protocol (LLDP)


Layer 2 Discovery Protocols :

	* Layer 2 discovery protocols such as CDP and LLDP share information with and discover information about neighboring
	  (connected) devices

	* Shared information includes Host-name, Ip address, Device type, etc

	* CDP is a cisco proprietary protocol

	* LLDP is an industry standard Protocol (IEEE 802.1AB)
			# IEEE 802 --> creates a unified set of protocols that devices adhere to for communication
	
	* CDP and LLDP can be considered a security risk because they share information about devices in the network
			# Admins have to decide weather or not to use them in the network or not
					

